1359
00:50:15,840 --> 00:50:16,840
Bai thought it was me.

1360
00:50:17,160 --> 00:50:18,160
I've got goosebumps.

1361
00:50:22,360 --> 00:50:22,920
Wait.

1362
00:50:24,640 --> 00:50:25,880
How could it be you?

1363
00:50:26,140 --> 00:50:27,820
(Exactly. How could it be you?)

1364
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:30,080
Our clues were hanging couplets
and setting off firecrackers.

1365
00:50:30,640 --> 00:50:32,480
I kept doing this for you.

1366
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:33,600
I was hanging them.

1367
00:50:34,080 --> 00:50:34,720
The right one.

1368
00:50:34,720 --> 00:50:35,640
The left one.

1369
00:50:35,640 --> 00:50:37,160
The banner on top.

1370
00:50:37,680 --> 00:50:38,440
You just ignored me.

1371
00:50:38,720 --> 00:50:39,840
Then I realized

1372
00:50:39,840 --> 00:50:40,680
you didn't recognize me.

1373
00:50:40,680 --> 00:50:41,520
You were setting off firecrackers.

1374
00:50:41,520 --> 00:50:42,840
Setting off firecrackers.

1375
00:50:42,840 --> 00:50:43,320
You lit them,

1376
00:50:43,320 --> 00:50:44,440
and I went boom.

1377
00:50:44,440 --> 00:50:46,200
You lit them, and I went boom.

1378
00:50:47,200 --> 00:50:48,520
I did that seven or eight times.

1379
00:50:48,520 --> 00:50:49,440
(You call that a boom?)

1380
00:50:49,440 --> 00:50:50,520
The clue was firecrackers.

1381
00:50:50,520 --> 00:50:52,000
You acted out a sparkler.

1382
00:50:53,400 --> 00:50:54,800
He really did get it wrong.

1383
00:50:57,560 --> 00:50:58,200
Bai.

1384
00:50:58,920 --> 00:50:59,560
When round two started,

1385
00:50:59,560 --> 00:51:01,200
I spent forever putting stuff
on the window.

1386
00:51:01,200 --> 00:51:01,920
What else would I be hanging?

1387
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:03,760
I was right here.

1388
00:51:04,680 --> 00:51:05,760
Horizontal and vertical.

1389
00:51:05,760 --> 00:51:07,400
I kept hanging them right here.

1390
00:51:07,400 --> 00:51:08,040
You were right here.

1391
00:51:08,040 --> 00:51:10,040
Know what Chengcheng was doing?

1392
00:51:10,040 --> 00:51:11,520
Setting off firecrackers
right in my face.

1393
00:51:11,980 --> 00:51:14,580
(Sorry, that was me)

1394
00:51:14,840 --> 00:51:17,040
I saw you out of the corner of my eye.

1395
00:51:17,040 --> 00:51:18,920
Who hangs couplets like that?

1396
00:51:21,440 --> 00:51:22,800
How's anyone supposed to know?

1397
00:51:23,280 --> 00:51:24,240
Then how should I do it?

1398
00:51:24,880 --> 00:51:26,360
Tell me how I should do it!

1399
00:51:28,840 --> 00:51:29,320
Huang Jingyu.

1400
00:51:31,160 --> 00:51:32,920
If you don't wanna leave Huairou,

1401
00:51:32,920 --> 00:51:33,560
just say so.

1402
00:51:35,600 --> 00:51:35,920
Wait.

1403
00:51:35,920 --> 00:51:37,880
Did you ever try
setting off firecrackers yourself?

1404
00:51:38,320 --> 00:51:39,320
I hadn't even hung the couplets.

1405
00:51:39,320 --> 00:51:40,360
Why would I set off firecrackers?

1406
00:51:40,360 --> 00:51:41,800
(At 33, he's obsessed
with doing things in order)

1407
00:51:41,800 --> 00:51:43,720
His house must be so organized.

1408
00:51:44,640 --> 00:51:45,840
You just wanted to set off firecrackers.

1409
00:51:45,840 --> 00:51:47,000
I just wanted to set off firecrackers.

1410
00:51:47,840 --> 00:51:49,360
I just wanted to hang couplets.

1411
00:51:49,360 --> 00:51:50,160
And he lit them.

1412
00:51:53,000 --> 00:51:53,880
I only had one thought.

1413
00:51:53,880 --> 00:51:54,760
He gets me.

1414
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:57,440
He was the only one
setting off firecrackers.

1415
00:52:00,800 --> 00:52:03,480
Let's congratulate Bing again

1416
00:52:03,480 --> 00:52:05,280
(Only Killer Bing completed his mission)
for being the smartest

1417
00:52:05,280 --> 00:52:06,320
of all the Clueless Killers.

1418
00:52:12,200 --> 00:52:13,720
Has Bai really outdone me?

1419
00:52:17,600 --> 00:52:17,920
It's fine.

1420
00:52:17,920 --> 00:52:19,920
All my stupidity stays at 32.

1421
00:52:20,300 --> 00:52:24,020
(Tomorrow, I'll
be a smarter 33-year-old)

1422
00:52:24,040 --> 00:52:25,680
You really know how to let things go.

1423
00:52:25,680 --> 00:52:26,520
(A positive attitude
makes all the difference)

1424
00:52:26,520 --> 00:52:27,600
People tend

1425
00:52:27,600 --> 00:52:28,960
to break their own records.

1426
00:52:28,960 --> 00:52:31,080
Bai, we've got firecrackers for you.

1427
00:52:32,960 --> 00:52:34,560
Enough to reach his front door.

1428
00:52:34,560 --> 00:52:36,480
Let's see how firecrackers
really go off.

1429
00:52:44,560 --> 00:52:45,320
Churan, you're so thoughtful.

1430
00:52:45,320 --> 00:52:45,920
It's not even New Year's yet.

1431
00:52:45,920 --> 00:52:47,400
Why'd you bring two boxes of Yili?

1432
00:52:47,400 --> 00:52:48,480
You looked exhausted from the game.

1433
00:52:48,480 --> 00:52:49,400
Thought you could use a boost.

1434
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:50,840
We Shandong folks
gotta look out for each other.

1435
00:52:50,840 --> 00:52:51,640
Now that's perfect.

1436
00:52:51,640 --> 00:52:53,320
Yili goes with everything.

1437
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:55,360
Then get Yili to back you up next time.

1438
00:52:55,680 --> 00:52:57,080
You gotta have a strategy to win.

1439
00:52:57,080 --> 00:52:57,720
With Yili,

1440
00:52:57,720 --> 00:52:59,400
anything goes.

1441
00:53:05,640 --> 00:53:06,040
Let's eat.

1442
00:53:07,960 --> 00:53:08,800
What's that?

1443
00:53:08,960 --> 00:53:09,800
He's got a bag.

1444
00:53:10,800 --> 00:53:11,120
A bag?

1445
00:53:11,720 --> 00:53:13,640
What's the rush? Where you going?

1446
00:53:14,080 --> 00:53:15,880
Rushing back to Chaoyang District?

1447
00:53:15,880 --> 00:53:16,960
It's part of my outfit.

1448
00:53:16,960 --> 00:53:17,940
(Fashion accessory)

1449
00:53:17,980 --> 00:53:19,080
(Keeping it real as always)

1450
00:53:19,080 --> 00:53:20,440
Is it for style or carrying stuff?

1451
00:53:20,440 --> 00:53:21,040
Style.

1452
00:53:21,040 --> 00:53:22,320
You're here to pack up leftovers?

1453
00:53:22,500 --> 00:53:22,860
(Fashion accessory)

1454
00:53:22,860 --> 00:53:23,980
(Practical accessory)

1455
00:53:26,220 --> 00:53:27,340
(Clay pot chicken stew)

1456
00:53:27,380 --> 00:53:28,460
(Pork ribs with dried green beans)

1457
00:53:28,500 --> 00:53:29,300
(Pepper chicken and seafood tofu)

1458
00:53:29,340 --> 00:53:29,980
(Braised pork with chestnuts)

1459
00:53:30,020 --> 00:53:30,900
(Celery hearts with nuts)

1460
00:53:30,940 --> 00:53:31,980
(Sturgeon and chestnut mousse)

1461
00:53:32,120 --> 00:53:33,800
(Sturgeon and chestnut meatballs)
Bai wanted to welcome everyone,

1462
00:53:33,800 --> 00:53:35,000
so he booked

1463
00:53:35,000 --> 00:53:37,040
a whole-lamb roasting expert in advance.

1464
00:53:40,240 --> 00:53:42,240
Thank you.

1465
00:53:42,240 --> 00:53:43,080
Thanks, Mr. Bai.

1466
00:53:43,080 --> 00:53:44,040
(Eat and drink up, everyone)

1467
00:53:44,040 --> 00:53:46,440
I carry on the traditional
pull-and-eat roast lamb technique.

1468
00:53:46,920 --> 00:53:49,160
With this pull-and-eat roast lamb,

1469
00:53:49,160 --> 00:53:51,740
(Liu Lei)
everyone needs to stand up.

1470
00:53:51,760 --> 00:53:53,160
Put on gloves
and pull off pieces to eat.

1471
00:53:53,440 --> 00:53:55,000
It's unlike any other roast lamb.

1472
00:53:55,320 --> 00:53:56,320
The first time I tried it,

1473
00:53:56,320 --> 00:53:57,680
we stood around all night,

1474
00:53:57,680 --> 00:53:58,600
pulling pieces off the lamb.

1475
00:53:59,080 --> 00:54:00,640
You keep circling around and eating.

1476
00:54:01,720 --> 00:54:03,480
(Standing roast lamb experience)
First, peel off the thin, crispy skin.

1477
00:54:04,040 --> 00:54:05,880
Round one is the crispy skin.

1478
00:54:05,880 --> 00:54:06,800
Round two is the meat.

1479
00:54:06,800 --> 00:54:08,480
It's juicy,
with just the right amount of fat.

1480
00:54:08,480 --> 00:54:10,000
Round three is the lamb ribs.

1481
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:11,520
They're beautifully charred
near the bone.

1482
00:54:11,520 --> 00:54:13,440
For round four, we use the leg meat

1483
00:54:13,440 --> 00:54:14,720
to make stuffed flatbread.

1484
00:54:14,720 --> 00:54:15,680
Round five is the bones.

1485
00:54:15,680 --> 00:54:16,680
Round six is the soup.

1486
00:54:16,680 --> 00:54:18,360
That's six dishes from one lamb.

1487
00:54:18,820 --> 00:54:19,660
(Mm-hmm)

1488
00:54:21,080 --> 00:54:21,600
It's pretty good.

1489
00:54:21,600 --> 00:54:22,120
Delicious.

1490
00:54:22,120 --> 00:54:22,680
Not bad.

1491
00:54:23,000 --> 00:54:24,280
(First round: Crispy skin)
It's crispiest beside the ribs.

1492
00:54:28,640 --> 00:54:30,160
Tastes like crispy pork cracklings.

1493
00:54:31,340 --> 00:54:32,060
(Wow)

1494
00:54:33,580 --> 00:54:34,340
(Mmm)

1495
00:54:35,660 --> 00:54:37,180
(Mmm)

1496
00:54:37,360 --> 00:54:38,320
The best way to describe it

1497
00:54:38,320 --> 00:54:39,840
is that the charred bits

1498
00:54:39,840 --> 00:54:41,440
taste just like pork cracklings.

1499
00:54:42,440 --> 00:54:43,400
Exactly the same texture.

1500
00:54:43,840 --> 00:54:45,200
(He knows his cracklings)
You gotta try this.

1501
00:54:45,200 --> 00:54:46,200
This is the tastiest part.

1502
00:54:46,760 --> 00:54:47,320
This one?

1503
00:54:47,560 --> 00:54:48,360
Try it. Trust me.

1504
00:54:48,960 --> 00:54:49,840
Be a good host.

1505
00:54:49,840 --> 00:54:50,680
Give him some.

1506
00:54:50,680 --> 00:54:52,240
Show some hospitality.

1507
00:54:52,240 --> 00:54:52,640
I am.

1508
00:54:52,640 --> 00:54:53,160
I'll feed you.

1509
00:54:53,160 --> 00:54:53,560
I am.

1510
00:54:53,560 --> 00:54:53,880
I'll feed you.

1511
00:54:53,880 --> 00:54:54,280
I have some.

1512
00:54:55,640 --> 00:54:56,160
No.

1513
00:54:56,160 --> 00:54:56,480
Eat mine.

1514
00:54:56,480 --> 00:54:57,240
(Local hospitality)
Here.

1515
00:54:57,240 --> 00:54:57,680
Feed me.

1516
00:54:57,680 --> 00:54:58,280
Come on.

1517
00:55:00,780 --> 00:55:02,700
(Carry on and fool around)

1518
00:55:04,960 --> 00:55:06,000
For round two,

1519
00:55:06,000 --> 00:55:07,280
our roast lamb is ready.

1520
00:55:07,280 --> 00:55:08,280
What you're seeing

1521
00:55:08,280 --> 00:55:09,640
is juicy, marbled lamb.

1522
00:55:10,560 --> 00:55:12,080
Why do I feel like I'm picking grapes?

1523
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:13,560
And that's

1524
00:55:13,560 --> 00:55:14,760
how pull-and-eat roast lamb

1525
00:55:14,760 --> 00:55:15,440
got its name.

1526
00:55:16,460 --> 00:55:18,540
(Second round: Juicy lamb)

1527
00:55:23,920 --> 00:55:25,400
Round three is the lamb ribs.

1528
00:55:25,400 --> 00:55:27,220
(Third round: Lamb ribs)
They're charred beautifully near the bone.

1529
00:55:30,520 --> 00:55:31,080
So good.

1530
00:55:32,940 --> 00:55:34,780
(Going to town on those ribs)

1531
00:55:37,520 --> 00:55:39,160
We're not playing any more games

1532
00:55:39,160 --> 00:55:40,520
where we blow
in each other's faces, right?

1533
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:42,800
Not after all that garlic and onion.

1534
00:55:42,800 --> 00:55:44,360
Now's the perfect time to blow.

1535
00:55:45,640 --> 00:55:46,960
That'll make your eyes water.

1536
00:55:46,960 --> 00:55:48,100
(Breath attack)

1537
00:55:54,920 --> 00:55:56,000
Wipe your mouth.

1538
00:55:56,000 --> 00:55:57,280
All that huffing and puffing.

1539
00:56:00,240 --> 00:56:00,520
Wait.

1540
00:56:00,520 --> 00:56:02,240
You've got some cumin stuck there.

1541
00:56:02,240 --> 00:56:02,800
Not your teeth.

1542
00:56:02,800 --> 00:56:03,440
Yeah, your lip.

1543
00:56:04,270 --> 00:56:04,920
God, you...

1544
00:56:04,920 --> 00:56:05,400
Yeah, right there.

1545
00:56:05,400 --> 00:56:05,840
You got it.

1546
00:56:06,680 --> 00:56:07,640
See? That was a big piece.

1547
00:56:12,360 --> 00:56:12,800
Delicious.

1548
00:56:13,960 --> 00:56:14,400
Jingyu,

1549
00:56:14,840 --> 00:56:15,880
want to try some fermented bean juice?

1550
00:56:15,880 --> 00:56:16,400
We've got some right here.

1551
00:56:16,920 --> 00:56:18,160
I'll give it a try.

1552
00:56:18,160 --> 00:56:19,120
Let's try it.

1553
00:56:19,120 --> 00:56:19,640
Me too.

1554
00:56:19,640 --> 00:56:20,400
I've never tried it.

1555
00:56:20,400 --> 00:56:21,160
I'm curious.

1556
00:56:21,560 --> 00:56:23,400
(Don't get it, but respect it)
You guys actually like this stuff?

1557
00:56:23,400 --> 00:56:24,440
How bad can it be?

1558
00:56:24,440 --> 00:56:25,520
That's what I want to know.

1559
00:56:25,920 --> 00:56:27,280
We've already tried it.

1560
00:56:27,280 --> 00:56:28,840
Let the first-timers have a go.

1561
00:56:28,840 --> 00:56:30,300
(Once was more than enough)
I've tried it too.

1562
00:56:30,560 --> 00:56:32,280
Look how tightly
he's clenching his fists.

1563
00:56:32,300 --> 00:56:33,140
(Those fists mean business)

1564
00:56:36,680 --> 00:56:38,040
Why are the cups different sizes?

1565
00:56:39,040 --> 00:56:39,360
Try some.

1566
00:56:39,360 --> 00:56:40,080
(Choose your cup size)

1567
00:56:40,080 --> 00:56:40,400
Yeah, try it.

1568
00:56:40,760 --> 00:56:41,640
You want some too?

1569
00:56:42,400 --> 00:56:43,120
Okay, I'll take a small one.

1570
00:56:43,120 --> 00:56:43,960
How about an extra-large?

1571
00:56:44,280 --> 00:56:44,800
Small one.

1572
00:56:47,200 --> 00:56:47,920
Here.

1573
00:56:48,100 --> 00:56:49,520
(You're here, so try it)
I've had it before.

1574
00:56:49,520 --> 00:56:50,240
You're not even from Beijing.

1575
00:56:50,240 --> 00:56:50,560
Quick.

1576
00:56:51,080 --> 00:56:52,240
Get Hu an extra-large.

1577
00:56:53,440 --> 00:56:54,760
Song just got back today.

1578
00:56:54,760 --> 00:56:56,240
How could I take that away from him?

1579
00:56:56,640 --> 00:56:57,440
Song, take it.

1580
00:56:57,740 --> 00:57:00,300
(Okay, that's a little too generous)

1581
00:57:00,320 --> 00:57:01,280
Only the big cups are left.

1582
00:57:02,280 --> 00:57:03,080
What? The biggest one?

1583
00:57:05,520 --> 00:57:06,080
Bai.

1584
00:57:06,080 --> 00:57:06,640
I can't do it.

1585
00:57:06,640 --> 00:57:07,600
(No one gets away)

1586
00:57:07,600 --> 00:57:08,160
I...

1587
00:57:08,160 --> 00:57:08,680
No, listen.

1588
00:57:09,360 --> 00:57:10,240
I've lived in Beijing my whole life.

1589
00:57:10,240 --> 00:57:11,040
Why would I drink this now?

1590
00:57:11,040 --> 00:57:11,840
Come on, Beijinger.

1591
00:57:19,200 --> 00:57:20,320
Does it taste like soy milk?

1592
00:57:20,940 --> 00:57:22,260
(Of course not!)

1593
00:57:29,180 --> 00:57:30,700
(The fermented bean juice is kicking in)

1594
00:57:30,920 --> 00:57:33,200
Tastes just like tofu.

1595
00:57:33,200 --> 00:57:34,880
(That's a wild claim)
There...

1596
00:57:34,880 --> 00:57:35,880
There's something wrong
with your taste buds.

1597
00:57:35,880 --> 00:57:36,680
You should get that checked.

1598
00:57:36,680 --> 00:57:37,720
Just like tofu?

1599
00:57:43,360 --> 00:57:44,040
Why is it so sour?

1600
00:57:45,520 --> 00:57:46,280
So sour.

1601
00:57:52,000 --> 00:57:53,720
It's nothing like what I expected.

1602
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:54,720
Is this stuff fermented?

1603
00:57:56,120 --> 00:57:57,120
We're not drinking it.

1604
00:57:57,120 --> 00:57:58,240
Can we just smell it?

1605
00:57:58,240 --> 00:57:59,160
Honestly, it doesn't smell bad.

1606
00:57:59,160 --> 00:58:00,280
It smells like soy milk.

1607
00:58:01,360 --> 00:58:01,920
Really?

1608
00:58:01,920 --> 00:58:02,640
More like tofu.

1609
00:58:02,640 --> 00:58:04,160
Actually, after a few sips...

1610
00:58:04,160 --> 00:58:04,600
Once you get used to it,

1611
00:58:04,600 --> 00:58:05,600
it's not that bad.

1612
00:58:05,960 --> 00:58:07,880
(I know exactly what you mean)
Smells like brined tofu.

1613
00:58:07,880 --> 00:58:10,000
It's definitely an acquired taste.

1614
00:58:10,000 --> 00:58:10,960
But somehow,

1615
00:58:10,960 --> 00:58:12,280
I keep wanting more.

1616
00:58:12,720 --> 00:58:14,120
Seriously?

1617
00:58:14,560 --> 00:58:15,040
I'm serious.

1618
00:58:16,200 --> 00:58:17,000
It's better on the second sip.

1619
00:58:17,560 --> 00:58:18,120
Right?

1620
00:58:18,600 --> 00:58:19,880
It's mostly just sour, right?

1621
00:58:19,880 --> 00:58:21,120
There's not much else to it.

1622
00:58:21,120 --> 00:58:21,640
Yeah.

1623
00:58:21,640 --> 00:58:24,120
There's a hint of sweetness at the end.

1624
00:58:24,220 --> 00:58:25,540
(Starting to savor the flavor)

1625
00:58:27,760 --> 00:58:28,760
What year is this tofu from?

1626
00:58:30,280 --> 00:58:31,860
(A century-old vintage... almost)
June, two years ago.

1627
00:58:32,120 --> 00:58:32,880
From the year 2000.

1628
00:58:33,760 --> 00:58:34,360
1900.

1629
00:58:36,400 --> 00:58:37,360
Song, did you have any?

1630
00:58:38,120 --> 00:58:40,040
