2325
01:20:33,640 --> 01:20:35,080
And you stopped him.

2326
01:20:35,280 --> 01:20:36,040
Nothing wrong with that.

2327
01:20:36,600 --> 01:20:37,720
Song did nothing wrong.

2328
01:20:37,720 --> 01:20:38,960
It's our turn, right?

2329
01:20:38,960 --> 01:20:39,440
Let's go.

2330
01:20:39,780 --> 01:20:41,820
(No info, No info, Undercover's
object: Arsenic, No info)

2331
01:20:43,000 --> 01:20:44,360
(Brainstorming)
What's your hometown known for? Think.

2332
01:20:44,360 --> 01:20:45,800
Walnuts and chestnuts.

2333
01:20:45,800 --> 01:20:46,480
Chestnuts?

2334
01:20:46,760 --> 01:20:47,880
(Undercover: Shen Teng, Answer: Arsenic)
Because Miyun...

2335
01:20:47,880 --> 01:20:48,640
Miyun's

2336
01:20:48,640 --> 01:20:49,040
big chestnuts.

2337
01:20:49,040 --> 01:20:50,320
(Huairou, Jingting)
Miyun's big chestnuts.

2338
01:20:52,280 --> 01:20:53,440
I'm from Huairou.

2339
01:20:54,460 --> 01:20:56,220
(Messed up again)

2340
01:20:56,220 --> 01:20:58,320
(Undercover: Shen Teng,
Answer: Arsenic)

2341
01:20:58,320 --> 01:20:59,800
(Quick damage control)
Huairou's sweet chestnuts.

2342
01:21:01,640 --> 01:21:03,000
(Whispering among themselves)
Do shoes count as objects?

2343
01:21:03,000 --> 01:21:04,960
(Happy to clarify)
Everything counts as an object.

2344
01:21:05,160 --> 01:21:05,880
That's one, right?

2345
01:21:06,760 --> 01:21:07,400
What?

2346
01:21:07,400 --> 01:21:09,180
(Innocent)

2347
01:21:13,300 --> 01:21:14,460
(Let's whisper)

2348
01:21:14,480 --> 01:21:15,320
Does a cabinet count as an object?

2349
01:21:15,320 --> 01:21:15,920
Yes.

2350
01:21:15,920 --> 01:21:16,620
(Blurts out the answer)

2351
01:21:17,960 --> 01:21:19,200
He was asking me.

2352
01:21:19,300 --> 01:21:20,780
(That doesn't count)

2353
01:21:25,360 --> 01:21:26,440
Bai, you go first.

2354
01:21:29,600 --> 01:21:31,360
We haven't done anything,
and we've wasted five questions.

2355
01:21:34,840 --> 01:21:36,160
Ask if it's edible.

2356
01:21:36,840 --> 01:21:37,840
Edible?

2357
01:21:37,840 --> 01:21:39,680
You'd eat anything when you're mad.

2358
01:21:43,680 --> 01:21:44,240
Chengcheng.

2359
01:21:51,740 --> 01:21:54,020
(What was I gonna ask again?)

2360
01:21:54,080 --> 01:21:55,600
Why'd you spin around?

2361
01:21:58,680 --> 01:22:00,800
Is it food?

2362
01:22:00,800 --> 01:22:02,120
(Questions used: 1)

2363
01:22:02,120 --> 01:22:02,680
No.

2364
01:22:03,960 --> 01:22:05,280
I mean...

2365
01:22:05,280 --> 01:22:06,040
Is it edible?

2366
01:22:06,560 --> 01:22:07,210
I already asked that.

2367
01:22:07,210 --> 01:22:09,260
(Quickly takes back a question)

2368
01:22:11,080 --> 01:22:13,440
I'm thinking about his question.

2369
01:22:13,920 --> 01:22:15,240
She's just thinking out loud.

2370
01:22:15,260 --> 01:22:16,540
(I get you)
Exactly.

2371
01:22:16,840 --> 01:22:18,360
You say every thought out loud.

2372
01:22:19,300 --> 01:22:20,780
(Thinking out loud)

2373
01:22:23,400 --> 01:22:24,940
(Hinting at its physical form)
Is it a liquid?

2374
01:22:29,640 --> 01:22:30,280
Song.

2375
01:22:30,540 --> 01:22:31,820
(Why's he looking at me?)

2376
01:22:32,040 --> 01:22:32,440
Who?

2377
01:22:33,560 --> 01:22:34,560
It's not Song. I mean...

2378
01:22:37,680 --> 01:22:38,720
We're looking at each other.

2379
01:22:38,720 --> 01:22:40,360
Why not just talk to me?

2380
01:22:40,360 --> 01:22:42,520
(Heartbroken)
My heart's dead. Why bother talking?

2381
01:22:42,520 --> 01:22:43,880
He's looking right at me
and calling me Song.

2382
01:22:43,880 --> 01:22:45,900
True heartbreak doesn't make a scene.

2383
01:22:45,900 --> 01:22:46,900
Hu.

2384
01:22:48,300 --> 01:22:51,580
Is it a liquid?

2385
01:22:51,580 --> 01:22:52,940
No.

2386
01:22:53,360 --> 01:22:54,120
It's dry.

2387
01:22:55,160 --> 01:22:56,160
It could be thick.

2388
01:22:57,680 --> 01:22:58,920
No, didn't he ask

2389
01:22:58,920 --> 01:23:00,000
if you could suck it?

2390
01:23:00,480 --> 01:23:01,440
(Different kinds of "xi")
No.

2391
01:23:01,440 --> 01:23:02,360
He meant watery.

2392
01:23:02,720 --> 01:23:03,980
Neither of those?

2393
01:23:03,980 --> 01:23:04,740
(Neither watery nor suckable)

2394
01:23:06,160 --> 01:23:08,640
I meant "xi" as in west.

2395
01:23:08,780 --> 01:23:10,540
(Watery, suck, west)

2396
01:23:10,580 --> 01:23:12,380
(Do I look amused to you?)

2397
01:23:14,240 --> 01:23:15,640
Eastern and western cultures.

2398
01:23:16,020 --> 01:23:17,140
(What a cunning undercover agent)

2399
01:23:17,140 --> 01:23:20,620
(His teammates are stunned)

2400
01:23:20,800 --> 01:23:23,720
Pizza, pasta...

2401
01:23:23,720 --> 01:23:25,240
My question was perfectly fine.

2402
01:23:25,240 --> 01:23:26,840
You made it complicated.

2403
01:23:28,320 --> 01:23:28,800
Fine.

2404
01:23:28,800 --> 01:23:29,920
Is it western?

2405
01:23:32,920 --> 01:23:33,920
I don't know.

2406
01:23:35,480 --> 01:23:37,760
That makes things difficult.

2407
01:23:40,280 --> 01:23:41,800
Then that question doesn't count, right?

2408
01:23:41,900 --> 01:23:44,180
(Can someone stop him?)

2409
01:23:46,520 --> 01:23:47,800
He didn't answer my question.

2410
01:23:48,560 --> 01:23:49,520
He said he didn't know.

2411
01:23:49,940 --> 01:23:52,100
(Can't bear to watch)

2412
01:23:54,920 --> 01:23:56,240
Even you can't stand me anymore.

2413
01:23:59,240 --> 01:24:00,480
Hu gave it all away.

2414
01:24:00,480 --> 01:24:03,040
He's left me speechless too, seriously.

2415
01:24:03,040 --> 01:24:04,120
We're asking one question,

2416
01:24:04,120 --> 01:24:05,160
but getting several answers.

2417
01:24:05,800 --> 01:24:07,000
And it doesn't even count.

2418
01:24:07,000 --> 01:24:08,820
(You're lucky to have a spy like me)

2419
01:24:09,780 --> 01:24:11,220
(Crying with laughter)

2420
01:24:14,640 --> 01:24:15,680
Hu, is it

2421
01:24:16,000 --> 01:24:17,040
a cool color?

2422
01:24:17,040 --> 01:24:18,220
(Questions asked: 2)

2423
01:24:18,220 --> 01:24:20,020
(Arsenic's color tone: Red)

2424
01:24:20,600 --> 01:24:21,080
No.

2425
01:24:22,280 --> 01:24:23,200
It's not a cool color.

2426
01:24:23,520 --> 01:24:24,560
Churan's getting obvious.

2427
01:24:24,900 --> 01:24:25,820
(Might know the word)

2428
01:24:26,340 --> 01:24:28,130
(Churan's pretty sharp)
Now we're talking about color tones.

2429
01:24:28,800 --> 01:24:29,800
I have a feeling

2430
01:24:30,840 --> 01:24:31,880
it's Churan.

2431
01:24:34,360 --> 01:24:35,280
Is it used at home?

2432
01:24:35,340 --> 01:24:36,800
(Questions asked: 3)

2433
01:24:36,800 --> 01:24:38,400
Well, not necessarily.

2434
01:24:38,400 --> 01:24:39,760
You could use it if you insisted.

2435
01:24:39,820 --> 01:24:41,620
(He's just getting revenge)

2436
01:24:44,760 --> 01:24:47,280
It's so satisfying
watching Bing get his revenge.

2437
01:24:47,280 --> 01:24:48,040
So satisfying.

2438
01:24:48,040 --> 01:24:49,000
That feels good.

2439
01:24:51,100 --> 01:24:53,260
(How can I give them a subtle hint?)

2440
01:24:53,360 --> 01:24:55,600
So it's not a household essential.

2441
01:24:55,600 --> 01:24:57,660
(Not food, warm color, nonessential)
It's something strange.

2442
01:24:57,700 --> 01:24:58,800
(Keyword detected: Strange)

2443
01:24:58,800 --> 01:24:59,960
Strange, exactly.

2444
01:25:00,880 --> 01:25:01,680
Because

2445
01:25:01,680 --> 01:25:02,760
whenever

2446
01:25:03,070 --> 01:25:04,080
someone brought it up,

2447
01:25:04,080 --> 01:25:04,560
everyone

2448
01:25:05,320 --> 01:25:06,880
started laughing.

2449
01:25:06,880 --> 01:25:07,540
(Trying to steer them)

2450
01:25:08,840 --> 01:25:10,320
So it must be something dangerous

2451
01:25:10,320 --> 01:25:11,480
that could hurt someone.

2452
01:25:11,620 --> 01:25:13,380
(A slight smirk)

2453
01:25:15,440 --> 01:25:16,080
Hu,

2454
01:25:16,720 --> 01:25:17,720
is it three characters?

2455
01:25:17,740 --> 01:25:18,460
(Still steering them)

2456
01:25:18,480 --> 01:25:19,080
(Not food, not watery or suckable,)
Yes.

2457
01:25:19,080 --> 01:25:19,820
(warm color, nonessential,
three characters)

2458
01:25:19,820 --> 01:25:20,540
(Questions asked: 4)

2459
01:25:22,160 --> 01:25:22,800
Rat poison.

2460
01:25:22,800 --> 01:25:24,100
(Steering them toward poison)

2461
01:25:26,920 --> 01:25:27,560
He's the spy.

2462
01:25:27,580 --> 01:25:28,480
(Teng is the prime suspect)

2463
01:25:28,480 --> 01:25:29,240
Go ahead and ask.

2464
01:25:30,280 --> 01:25:31,200
Is it rat poison?

2465
01:25:31,200 --> 01:25:31,880
No.

2466
01:25:31,880 --> 01:25:34,560
(Questions asked: 5)

2467
01:25:34,560 --> 01:25:35,200
Cockroach poison.

2468
01:25:35,220 --> 01:25:36,340
(Still steering them)

2469
01:25:36,340 --> 01:25:37,720
Factory-direct cockroach poison,

2470
01:25:37,720 --> 01:25:38,520
ant poison,

2471
01:25:39,560 --> 01:25:40,280
and glue traps.

2472
01:25:41,400 --> 01:25:42,640
Wait, let me give you a tip.

2473
01:25:42,640 --> 01:25:44,280
You spies don't have to blow your cover,

2474
01:25:44,280 --> 01:25:46,760
but at least sum up the clues
for your teammates.

2475
01:25:47,320 --> 01:25:48,480
(Mr. Huang completely missed the hint)
So we have spies among us?

2476
01:25:48,480 --> 01:25:49,040
Yes.

2477
01:25:49,380 --> 01:25:51,820
(He's been summing things up all along)

2478
01:25:52,560 --> 01:25:53,280
Dried rat.

2479
01:25:53,920 --> 01:25:54,960
What would you do with a dried rat?

2480
01:25:55,920 --> 01:25:57,080
You could use it if you insisted.

2481
01:25:57,380 --> 01:25:59,020
(He's just here to cause trouble)

2482
01:25:59,480 --> 01:26:00,840
Well, you actually could.

2483
01:26:00,840 --> 01:26:01,800
Soak it in liquor?

2484
01:26:02,400 --> 01:26:03,600
No, I mean that dried rat...

2485
01:26:03,620 --> 01:26:05,580
(This is the one)
Look at my eyes.

2486
01:26:05,920 --> 01:26:07,720
Is it something

2487
01:26:08,240 --> 01:26:10,800
(Questions asked: 6)
you'd use in an emergency?

2488
01:26:11,520 --> 01:26:12,080
Yes.

2489
01:26:12,680 --> 01:26:14,580
So it's an emergency item.

2490
01:26:14,580 --> 01:26:15,380
(Clues: Not food, not watery
or suckable, warm color)

2491
01:26:15,380 --> 01:26:16,020
(Nonessential,
three characters, emergency item)

2492
01:26:16,300 --> 01:26:17,540
(Can't give myself away)

2493
01:26:17,580 --> 01:26:19,180
(Whoever gets it is in trouble)

2494
01:26:19,600 --> 01:26:20,640
Is it for household use?

2495
01:26:20,640 --> 01:26:22,080
You could use it if you insisted.

2496
01:26:22,080 --> 01:26:23,160
It must be something

2497
01:26:23,160 --> 01:26:24,760
dangerous that could hurt someone.

2498
01:26:25,080 --> 01:26:25,760
Rat poison.

2499
01:26:26,400 --> 01:26:27,200
Arsenic.

2500
01:26:31,080 --> 01:26:32,610
(Questions asked: 7)
Is it arsenic?

2501
01:26:32,640 --> 01:26:33,200
Yes.

2502
01:26:34,720 --> 01:26:35,240
Yes.

2503
01:26:35,260 --> 01:26:38,260
(Pretending to be shocked)

2504
01:26:38,680 --> 01:26:39,280
Nice one, Churan.

2505
01:26:39,280 --> 01:26:40,620
(Finally being clever)

2506
01:26:40,720 --> 01:26:41,560
Now guess who the spy is.

2507
01:26:41,560 --> 01:26:42,400
We haven't guessed the spy yet.

2508
01:26:42,800 --> 01:26:43,240
Teng.

2509
01:26:43,340 --> 01:26:44,960
(Spy identified: Shen Teng)
(Correct! No surprise there.)

2510
01:26:44,960 --> 01:26:46,680
But you gave some really good hints.

2511
01:26:46,680 --> 01:26:47,360
Rat poison.

2512
01:26:47,360 --> 01:26:48,520
That was a good one.

2513
01:26:49,080 --> 01:26:51,080
No, this thing is just too hard
to give hints for.

2514
01:26:51,540 --> 01:26:52,980
(I know exactly how that feels)

2515
01:26:53,120 --> 01:26:54,400
(Team Shen Teng 3:3 Team Jia Bing)
The final score is...

2516
01:26:54,400 --> 01:26:55,760
three to three. It's a tie.

2517
01:26:58,680 --> 01:26:59,000
Let's go.

2518
01:27:51,660 --> 01:27:53,100
(Next episode: Undercover Werewolf)

2519
01:27:53,120 --> 01:27:54,000
Killer Zero

2520
01:27:54,000 --> 01:27:55,480
cannot eliminate good players directly

2521
01:27:55,480 --> 01:27:57,080
but can infect any good player

2522
01:27:57,080 --> 01:27:58,000
(Only Killer One can eliminate the good)
and turn them into Killer One.

2523
01:27:58,000 --> 01:27:59,520
(Killer Zero)
Killer, infect me!

2524
01:27:59,520 --> 01:28:00,380
(How a 33-year-old applies for a job)

2525
01:28:01,360 --> 01:28:02,560
What's the point of living

2526
01:28:02,560 --> 01:28:03,560
if I never get the Killer card?

2527
01:28:03,620 --> 01:28:05,380
(Completely unbothered)

2528
01:28:06,680 --> 01:28:07,720
Please infect me. I'm begging you.

2529
01:28:07,720 --> 01:28:08,520
It's not me.

2530
01:28:08,520 --> 01:28:09,040
Chengcheng.

2531
01:28:09,040 --> 01:28:09,960
Just name your target. I'll kill them.

2532
01:28:09,960 --> 01:28:10,600
I'll do it right away.

2533
01:28:10,700 --> 01:28:11,660
(Since you asked so nicely...)

2534
01:28:11,720 --> 01:28:12,560
Kill Hu.

2535
01:28:13,520 --> 01:28:15,040
Why does your infection move

2536
01:28:15,040 --> 01:28:16,000
look so lame?

2537
01:28:16,320 --> 01:28:16,920
Seriously?

2538
01:28:16,920 --> 01:28:17,560
Let me try.

2539
01:28:18,640 --> 01:28:19,320
What are you doing?

2540
01:28:19,340 --> 01:28:20,540
(Honking with laughter)

2541
01:28:20,800 --> 01:28:21,800
What a big dummy!

2542
01:28:22,520 --> 01:28:23,440
Do it with me.

2543
01:28:23,460 --> 01:28:24,640
(Are you picking me, Mr. Killer?)

2544
01:28:24,640 --> 01:28:25,040
Okay.

2545
01:28:27,640 --> 01:28:28,360
Kill...

2546
01:28:28,360 --> 01:28:28,840
Jia Bing.

2547
01:28:30,600 --> 01:28:31,920
Wait, it's really that simple?

2548
01:28:32,060 --> 01:28:33,100
(He's already been fooled once)

2549
01:28:33,800 --> 01:28:35,000
This room.

2550
01:28:36,060 --> 01:28:37,420
(Saw the whole thing)

2551
01:28:37,420 --> 01:28:38,060
(Ah!)

2552
01:28:38,560 --> 01:28:39,520
Wasn't it you who did it?

2553
01:28:39,520 --> 01:28:41,200
It wasn't me! It was him!

2554
01:28:41,200 --> 01:28:41,840
How could he have done it?

2555
01:28:41,840 --> 01:28:42,720
He came in behind me.

2556
01:28:42,720 --> 01:28:44,200
He was right in front of me.
I was watching him!

2557
01:28:44,200 --> 01:28:45,040
What were you watching?

2558
01:28:45,040 --> 01:28:45,800
You were outside!

2559
01:28:45,800 --> 01:28:46,880
I saw him right in front of me!

2560
01:28:46,880 --> 01:28:47,600
Oh, give me a break!

2561
01:28:47,600 --> 01:28:48,520
I was watching him!

2562
01:28:48,520 --> 01:28:50,440
Don't they sound like old ladies
arguing in the village?

2563
01:28:50,440 --> 01:28:52,160
Exactly! I told you he's a bad guy!

2564
01:28:52,160 --> 01:28:53,720
He's an exposed werewolf.
What's he afraid of?

2565
01:28:53,720 --> 01:28:55,040
He's playing mind games.

2566
01:28:55,360 --> 01:28:56,240
Let's start filming.

2567
01:28:56,740 --> 01:28:59,460
(First day at 33, life is peaceful)

2568
01:29:00,000 --> 01:29:01,120
It's Bai's birthday today.

2569
01:29:02,160 --> 01:29:03,680
Let's wish him a happy birthday.

2570
01:29:04,440 --> 01:29:06,400
Happy birthday, Bai!

2571
01:29:07,120 --> 01:29:08,480
(Back to the point)
Killer Zero is really clever.

2572
01:29:08,480 --> 01:29:09,480
Is he really that clever?

2573
01:29:09,480 --> 01:29:11,040
Or are some people just dumb?

2574
01:29:12,120 --> 01:29:12,880
I think

2575
01:29:12,880 --> 01:29:13,840
Hu is a bit suspicious too.

2576
01:29:14,280 --> 01:29:14,920
Churan,

2577
01:29:14,920 --> 01:29:15,480
you were

2578
01:29:15,480 --> 01:29:16,880
the only one I defended just now.

2579
01:29:16,880 --> 01:29:19,280
Yet you insisted on voting me out!

2580
01:29:20,160 --> 01:29:21,280
I'm only 26,

2581
01:29:21,280 --> 01:29:23,080
and my blood pressure's
already through the roof!

2582
01:29:24,980 --> 01:29:26,240
(Clueless Killer on the dance floor)
DJ, drop the beat!

2583
01:29:26,240 --> 01:29:27,920
(Bonus episode preview)
The DJ just can't catch the beat.

2584
01:29:27,920 --> 01:29:29,040
(Teng's Take: DJ Can't Catch the Beat)
The DJ just can't find the beat.

2585
01:29:29,040 --> 01:29:30,280
Northeast China's signature hype rap.

2586
01:29:35,180 --> 01:29:36,020
(Staring)

2587
01:29:36,060 --> 01:29:37,220
(Little Chinese Chef
serves everyone dumplings)

2588
01:29:37,220 --> 01:29:38,180
(Serving dumplings)

2589
01:29:38,180 --> 01:29:39,500
(Trying hard to swing and point)

2590
01:29:39,700 --> 01:29:41,120
(Didn't recognize the boss!)

2591
01:29:41,120 --> 01:29:42,800
Armed Killer's identity
is out in the open.

2592
01:29:42,920 --> 01:29:43,880
Out in the open?

2593
01:29:43,880 --> 01:29:45,960
No wonder that cowardly wolf
won't show himself.

2594
01:29:46,300 --> 01:29:47,480
(Coward)

2595
01:29:47,480 --> 01:29:48,280
Have you played this before?

2596
01:29:48,680 --> 01:29:49,320
(Innocent)
Yes.

2597
01:29:49,320 --> 01:29:49,800
Yes.

2598
01:29:50,080 --> 01:29:51,240
(Getting defensive)
What's that supposed to mean, Song?

2599
01:29:51,520 --> 01:29:52,660
(His devilish side takes over)
Doesn't look like it.

2600
01:29:52,680 --> 01:29:55,160
There must be a parallel universe
where we win.

2601
01:29:55,240 --> 01:29:55,960
What universe?

2602
01:29:55,960 --> 01:29:57,560
A parallel universe.

2603
01:29:58,320 --> 01:30:00,200
I heard "WeTV Universe".

2604
01:30:00,320 --> 01:30:02,440
I thought he sure knows how to flatter!

2605
01:30:02,440 --> 01:30:04,860
(Werewolf Disco Party:
DJ Can't Catch the Beat)

2606
01:30:04,860 --> 01:30:05,800
Creative Guessing Game.

2607
01:30:05,800 --> 01:30:07,280
Can you bring this onto a plane?

2608
01:30:07,280 --> 01:30:07,720
Legally

2609
01:30:07,720 --> 01:30:08,160
yes.

2610
01:30:08,440 --> 01:30:09,280
I don't mean checked luggage.

2611
01:30:09,280 --> 01:30:10,580
(Trying to get a clear answer)
I mean carrying it onto the plane.

2612
01:30:10,600 --> 01:30:11,680
How many questions are you asking?

2613
01:30:12,600 --> 01:30:13,360
Is it three characters?

2614
01:30:13,360 --> 01:30:14,200
By three characters,

2615
01:30:14,200 --> 01:30:15,720
(No loopholes allowed)
I don't mean the phrase itself.

2616
01:30:15,840 --> 01:30:16,360
What?

2617
01:30:16,360 --> 01:30:17,440
(He's pretty alert)
I wouldn't have thought of that.

2618
01:30:18,760 --> 01:30:19,880
Can you carry it around?

2619
01:30:19,880 --> 01:30:20,200
Take it along?

2620
01:30:20,200 --> 01:30:21,200
To sling across?

2621
01:30:21,600 --> 01:30:23,020
(Now that's a deep question)
Or to take along?

2622
01:30:23,560 --> 01:30:24,760
Or you mean shoelace?

2623
01:30:24,760 --> 01:30:26,400
Just answer yes or no.

2624
01:30:26,400 --> 01:30:27,440
(Got you, spy!)
Is it you?

2625
01:30:27,480 --> 01:30:28,080
No.

2626
01:30:28,300 --> 01:30:29,940
(More wild guesses coming your way!)

2627
